 The runner enforces **one shared output-byte budget for stdout and stderr combined** on every invocation, including the runtime version probe. Splitting output across two streams must not double the permitted capture. Going over the aggregate cap fails closed with `native_campaign_output_budget_exceeded`; retained evidence still excludes raw output. The timeout applies to the **entire process lifecycle**, including concurrent stdout/stderr drain completion. If an exited launcher leaves descendants holding inherited pipes open, the runner terminates the POSIX process group and cancels remaining read tasks when the deadline expires; no late pipe EOF can turn that campaign into PASS.
 
